name: Wave 4C — text substitutions (formatters, conditional, loop)
description: ```
A fenced `bind … = \`\`\` … \`\`\`` template body composes a `[for each]`
loop, an `[if]`/`[otherwise]` conditional, and `{{ expr as a <formatter> }}`
interpolations against every formatter `FormatterRegistry` recognizes
(`integer`, `decimal(N)`, `short date`, `long date`). The source is an
external file (not `source_inline`) because its fenced template body itself
uses `\`\`\`` delimiters, which would collide with `source_inline`'s own
fence-closing rule.
```
tags: inform7, wave4, templates, formatters, codegen

source: wave4_4c_templates.meridian

expect_compile: pass
expect_swift_not_contains: _unresolved
expect_swift_contains: for __item in
expect_swift_contains: meridianFormat(__item.member("score") ?? .null, as: "integer")
expect_swift_contains: meridianFormat(__item.member("score") ?? .null, as: "decimal(2)")
expect_swift_contains: meridianFormat(.date(Date()), as: "short date")
expect_swift_contains: meridianFormat(.date(Date()), as: "long date")
expect_swift_contains: private func meridianFormat
